From: Aliensense <nxs@aliensense.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] media: simaai-v4l2-video: set a capture node's format on its own channel

vidioc_s_fmt_vid_cap() sets the DMA bridge's format on pad 0, stream 0,
whatever channel the node captures. The bridge stores it as channel 0's
format and passes it to the receiver's first pixel interface. A node of
channel 1 therefore overwrites channel 0's format, and two channels carrying
different codes, such as a monochrome Y10 camera beside a Bayer one, leave
channel 0 with the code of whichever node was set last: its STREAMON fails
with a code mismatch. Set the format on the channel's own sink pad and
stream, so each node sets its channel and its pixel interface alone.

---
 drivers/media/platform/simaai/simaai-v4l2-video.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/simaai/simaai-v4l2-video.c b/drivers/media/platform/simaai/simaai-v4l2-video.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/simaai/simaai-v4l2-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/simaai/simaai-v4l2-video.c
@@ -353,7 +353,14 @@
 	fmt.format.width = dev_fmt_pix->width;
 	fmt.format.height = dev_fmt_pix->height;
 	fmt.which = V4L2_SUBDEV_FORMAT_ACTIVE;
-	fmt.pad = 0;
+	/*
+	 * The node captures the bridge's channel ep_pad - VDMA_CHANNELS, whose
+	 * sink is the pad and the stream of that number. Pad 0 would set
+	 * channel 0's format, and the receiver's first pixel interface, whatever
+	 * channel the node captures.
+	 */
+	fmt.pad = dev->ep_pad - VDMA_CHANNELS;
+	fmt.stream = dev->ep_pad - VDMA_CHANNELS;
 	fmt.format.field = dev_fmt_pix->field;
 
 	ret = v4l2_subdev_call_state_active(dev->ep_sd, pad, set_fmt, &fmt);
